meta {
  name: 16. Cleanup - Delete DataSource
  type: http
  seq: 41
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasources/:id
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: {{sagaDataSourceId}}
}

tests {
  test("DataSource deleted or already gone", function() {
    const status = res.getStatus();
    // 204=deleted, 404=already gone, 400=wrong state, 409=has linked pipelines
    expect(status === 204 || status === 404 || status === 400 || status === 409).to.be.true;
  });
}

docs {
  **Saga step 16 of 18** — Delete the datasource (cleanup).

  Removes the MQTT datasource created in step 1. The pipeline must have been deleted first (step 15); a 409 is returned if linked pipelines still exist.

  **Expected Response:** 204 No Content. 404 if already deleted. 409 if linked pipelines still exist (delete pipeline first). 400 if wrong state.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | DataSource record removed from `portal_backend` DB |
  | Config Adapter | — |
  | External System | — |
}
